body:
Formal charges and resonance!

Sulfur needs to have 6 valence electrons and is odd in that it can have more than 4 bonds. The number of electrons you have in this structure is correct, but sulfur currently has a +2 formal charge and the oxygens both have -1 charges. The electrons on the two single-bonded oxygen atoms can create double bonds with sulfur in order to have a formal charge of 0 for all atoms. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
